          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Cold patch asphalt works — <strong class="text-white">compaction is what separates a repair that lasts years from one that pops out in weeks.</strong> Clean the hole, cut vertical edges, fill in thin lifts, and tamp each one properly (rent a plate compactor if you can). Done right, it's a legitimate multi-year fix for potholes and localized damage. It is not a fix for a failed subbase or widespread structural cracking — for that, you need hot mix or a full section rebuild, no matter how well you pack the patch.
